<title>SPAIN: Spanish 1998 budget - Economic forecasts detailed.</title>
<headline>Spanish 1998 budget - Economic forecasts detailed.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Spanish government is basing its 1998  budget on the following economic assumptions: (figures are percentage  changes unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>					    1998		   1997</p>
<p> Nominal GDP			     5.7		   5.2</p>
<p> Real GDP				  3.4		   3.2</p>
<p> Private consumption		   3.1		   3.0</p>
<p> Public consumption		    1.1		  -0.8</p>
<p> Gross capital formation	     7.6		   4.4</p>
<p>    - constuction			5.0		   1.2</p>
<p>    - capital goods		   11.5		   9.6</p>
<p>    - stock changed		    0.0		   0.0</p>
<p> Total internal demand		 3.8		   2.7</p>
<p> Exports				   9.9		  10.0</p>
<p> Imports				  10.6		   8.0</p>
<p>Trade balance (contribution to GDP)</p>
<p>					    -0.4		  0.4</p>
<p> CPI					 2.1		  2.2</p>
<p>NOTE - 1998 figures given out by Economy Ministry with revised 1997  forecasts.</p>
<p>--Madrd Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
</text>
